    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>📚 Read the <a href=\"https://www.plugixa.com/documentation/plugixa-team\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\"><strong>Plugixa Team Documentation</strong></a></p>\n<p>Plugixa Team is a modern team member management plugin for WordPress. Manage your<br />\nstaff and showcase your team on the frontend — all from a fast admin<br />\npanel.</p>\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>admin panel for managing team members and groups</li>\n<li>Skills and social links per member</li>\n<li>Grid and list frontend layouts with live-preview display views</li>\n<li>Group navigation, filtering, and client-side pagination</li>\n<li>Schema.org structured data (Person/Organization JSON-LD) with Yoast/Rank Math integration</li>\n<li>Shortcodes and a Gutenberg block for placing teams anywhere</li>\n<li>Multilingual support (WPML and Polylang)</li>\n<li>Translation-ready (<code>plugixa-team</code> text domain)</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin ZIP via <strong>Plugins <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Add New <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Upload Plugin</strong>, or extract it into<br />\n   wp-content/plugins/.</li>\n<li>Activate <strong>Plugixa Team</strong> through the <strong>Plugins</strong> menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Open the <strong>Plugixa Team</strong> admin menu to add team members and create display views.</li>\n<li>Place a team on any page using the provided shortcode or the Gutenberg block.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"which%20wordpress%20and%20php%20versions%20are%20required%3F\">\nWhich WordPress and PHP versions are required?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>WordPress 6.5 or later and PHP 8.0 or later.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20work%20with%20the%20block%20editor%3F\">\nDoes it work with the block editor?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Plugixa Team provides a Gutenberg block in addition to shortcodes.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"how%20do%20i%20display%20a%20team%20on%20the%20frontend%3F\">\nHow do I display a team on the frontend?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Create a display view in the admin, then insert its shortcode or the Plugixa Team block<br />\non any page or post.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "A modern team member management plugin with a admin panel, skills, social links, groups, and grid/list display layouts.",
    "description": "<p>📚 Read the <a href=\"https://www.plugixa.com/documentation/plugixa-team\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\"><strong>Plugixa Team Documentation</strong></a></p>\n<p>Plugixa Team is a modern team member management plugin for WordPress. Manage your<br />\nstaff and showcase your team on the frontend — all from a fast admin<br />\npanel.</p>\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>admin panel for managing team members and groups</li>\n<li>Skills and social links per member</li>\n<li>Grid and list frontend layouts with live-preview display views</li>\n<li>Group navigation, filtering, and client-side pagination</li>\n<li>Schema.org structured data (Person/Organization JSON-LD) with Yoast/Rank Math integration</li>\n<li>Shortcodes and a Gutenberg block for placing teams anywhere</li>\n<li>Multilingual support (WPML and Polylang)</li>\n<li>Translation-ready (<code>plugixa-team</code> text domain)</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "download_link": "https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/plugixa-team.1.0.0.zip",
